% ============================================================================
% synonyms.query.adj — a worked recall over the word-synonyms library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what is a synonym of
% happy?": it states no fact of its own — it only `import`s the grounded table
% and asks binding queries. The engine resolves each `?` against the `synonym`
% rows and returns EVERY synonym + the table's source/locator/trust (as of
% this cycle's extension, a bound word recalls MULTIPLE synonyms — `happy`
% now recalls cheerful ; content ; delighted ; ... ; merry, not just one). A
% word the table does not carry abstains honestly — the engine never invents
% a synonym.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli synonyms.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "synonyms.adj"

? synonym(happy, $Word)        % expect cheerful ; content ; delighted ; elated ; exultant ; glad ; joyful ; jubilant ; merry
? synonym(quick, $Word)        % expect fast ; speedy ; rapid ; swift
? synonym(smart, $Word)        % expect bright ; capable ; sophisticated ; witty (added this cycle)
? synonym(purple, $Word)       % expect abstain — no synonym is shipped for purple
